We conducted a study to replicate and extend the results of Levinson et al. (
2014
), who validated a breath-counting task as an objective measure of trait mindfulness. In line with the original study, we found good test-retest reliability of performance on the BCT, as well as correlations with sustained attention and self-reported mindfulness.

